{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4793446","formula":"C₁₁H₁₁⁺","hill":"C11H11","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":11.0,"H":11.0},"names":{"en":"Armilenium"},"descriptions":{"en":"Armilenium is a C11H+11 carbocation and was originally proposed as the first entirely organic sandwich compound. Named for its resemblance to an armillary sphere, NMR evidence for the carbocation was first described by Melvin J. Goldstein and Stanley A. Klein at Cornell University in 1973. In subsequent 13C NMR experiments by Goldstein and Joseph P. Dinnocenzo in 1984, the C11H+11 carbocation was generated under stable ion conditions at lower temperature and at higher magnetic field than previously possible."},"fame":2,"pubchemCid":12662406,"mass":143.2,"charge":1,"smiles":"C1=CC2C3C=CC4C2C4C3[CH+]1","inchikey":"YHLLCJAAILLOIR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"12662406","atoms":22,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.455,"y":0.111,"z":0.302,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.716,"y":-0.698,"z":1.082,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.235,"y":-0.899,"z":0.806,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.013,"y":-0.89,"z":-0.752,"el":"C"},{"x":1.45,"y":-1.164,"z":-1.072,"el":"C"},{"x":2.339,"y":-0.363,"z":-0.457,"el":"C"},{"x":1.843,"y":0.685,"z":0.453,"el":"C"},{"x":0.582,"y":0.335,"z":1.224,"el":"C"},{"x":0.504,"y":1.3,"z":0.077,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.345,"y":0.624,"z":-1.013,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.83,"y":0.826,"z":-0.792,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.511,"y":0.273,"z":0.493,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.159,"y":-1.215,"z":1.927,"el":"H"},{"x":0.136,"y":-1.818,"z":1.271,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.665,"y":-1.584,"z":-1.293,"el":"H"},{"x":1.737,"y":-1.955,"z":-1.752,"el":"H"},{"x":3.407,"y":-0.473,"z":-0.615,"el":"H"},{"x":2.584,"y":1.313,"z":0.932,"el":"H"},{"x":0.447,"y":0.678,"z":2.237,"el":"H"},{"x":0.313,"y":2.346,"z":0.254,"e